    "result_text": "Only one test class exists, and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` with two minimal, low-impact edits:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(owner.getCustomerCode() + \\\"-M\\\" + String.format(\\\"%02d\\\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))\")\n   ```\n\n### Why this keeps structural impact low\nThe derivation lives in the mapper as a single-line MapStruct expression rather than as a new method on the `Owner` entity. `Owner` is a large class (high WMC), so any method touched there would multiply the change cost by the whole class's complexity. `OwnerMapper` is a tiny interface with near-zero surrounding complexity, and the existing `toOwnerDto` method's cyclomatic complexity stays at 1 (the logic is a single expression, no branches). This mirrors the existing `displayName` computed-field pattern, so it's idiomatic for the codebase.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass.",
